Safe by default: the captcha fails closed (an unreachable verifier rejects the token) and lockout keys are stored
hashed. The captcha is OFF until `secret-key` is set, and then `VerifyAsync` returns true, so refuse to boot in
Production yourself if you require one. Never lock by user name alone: combine it with the client address and add
a budget per address.
```yaml
altruist:
  security:
    lockout:
      store: memory            # memory (default) | backplane (shared by the fleet)
    captcha:
      provider: turnstile      # turnstile | hcaptcha | recaptcha
      site-key: "0x4AAAA..."   # public, the client widget uses it
      secret-key: ""           # from ALTRUIST__SECURITY__CAPTCHA__SECRET_KEY
```
```csharp
var userKey = $"login:{name.ToLowerInvariant()}|{clientIp}";
var locked = await lockout.LockedForAsync(userKey);
if (locked > TimeSpan.Zero) throw new HttpApiException(429, "locked", "Too many failed attempts.");

if (!hasher.Verify(password, account?.PasswordHash))
{
    await lockout.RecordFailureAsync(userKey, 5, TimeSpan.FromMinutes(15), TimeSpan.FromMinutes(15));
    throw new HttpApiException(401, "invalid_credentials", "Invalid username or password.");
}
await lockout.ClearAsync(userKey);

if (captcha.Enabled && !await captcha.VerifyAsync(body.CaptchaToken ?? "", HttpContext.ClientIp()))
    throw new HttpApiException(400, "captcha_failed", "The security check failed.", "captcha");
```

Safe by default: only the SHA-256 of a ticket is stored, redemption is an atomic take (a second use fails), and
request log lines that contain the ticket URL are reduced to warnings (`redact-request-logs: true`). Write the
issuing endpoint yourself so your own rules (bans, maintenance) apply.
```yaml
altruist:
  security:
    tickets:
      query-param: ticket
      ttl-seconds: 30
      max-per-principal: 4
      session-hours: 12
      redact-request-logs: true
```
```csharp
[ApiController, Route("api"), Authorize]
public sealed class TicketController(IConnectionTicketService tickets) : ControllerBase
{
    [HttpPost("ticket")]
    public async Task<IActionResult> Ticket(CancellationToken ct)
    {
        var id = User.PrincipalId() ?? throw new UnauthorizedAccessException();
        var t = await tickets.IssueAsync(id, groupKey: User.PrincipalName(), ct);
        return Ok(new { ticket = t.Ticket, expiresIn = t.ExpiresInSeconds });
    }
}

[Portal("/game")]
[TicketShield]
public class GamePortal : AltruistPortal { }
